From a724ffb612e30c2df67bc33129c6f65b5582682d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:47:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] tu: implement VK_QCOM_rotated_copy_commands

The 2D engine can rotate while it copies, so buffer/image copies and most
rotated blits just set the rotation on the 2D blit. A blit that also
mirrors one axis at 90 or 270 degrees, or uses a cubic filter, goes
through the 3D path, which swaps the texture coordinates in the shader.
---
 docs/features.txt                     |   1 +
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_clear_blit.cc | 266 +++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc     |   1 +
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.h      |   2 +
 4 files changed, 248 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

